Were you displaced or invisible?  In those cases, the crocodile was
fleeing from where it thought you were by running in another
direction... which happened to be in the direction you actually were. 
Moving into a square is universally assumed to be attacking that
square, so if it was fleeing from your image and happened to bump into
the real you, you were attacked.

Now, if you scribbled Elbereth on the ground with your fingers, it
would flee away from that spot.  Even though it's quickly obfuscated,
scribbling in the dust is often good enough to give you a round or two
to do something productive.

